Context and Constraints

Context

Context is information that helps an AI understand your situation.

Without context

Create a workout plan.

The AI has very little information.

With context

Create a beginner workout plan.

Context:
I am new to exercise.
I have 30 minutes available each day.
I have access to basic gym equipment.

The AI now has more information to work with.

Constraints

Constraints tell the AI what limits or rules to follow.

Examples:

Keep the answer under 300 words.

Use simple language.

Give exactly five examples.

Do not use technical terminology without explaining it.

Why Context and Constraints Matter

Without clear requirements, an AI may produce a response that is technically relevant but not useful for your situation.

For example:

Write a study plan.

could produce almost anything.

Instead:

Create a 14-day study plan for a beginner learning HTML.

I can study for 45 minutes each evening.

Include:
- One topic per day
- A short explanation
- One practice task

Present it as a table.

This gives the AI a clearer target.

Important

More instructions do not automatically mean a better prompt.

Avoid adding unnecessary information.

Give the AI the information that actually helps it complete the task.